{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015159-nagah-venom-holy-cow-also-kitsune-help","id":1015159,"title":"Nagah Venom, holy cow! Also Kitsune help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-09T22:02:05-08:00","id":1015159,"title":"Nagah Venom, holy cow! Also Kitsune help","content":"Hello it's me again with that mixed breed chronicle I've been working on. This time I've sorted out everything regarding combat...well sorta I still need to structure my action better (newbie here). I have a few questions regarding my players characters.<br /> Firstly my Nagah player is enjoying his venom quite a bit. But I need ideas for how to challenge him as it seems like his venom does a lot of damage. I know that maybe normal, but it makes finding enemies for them fairly difficult if only he can poison them and kill them quickly.<br /> So any enemy suggestions?<br /> <br /> Secondly, I have a Kitsune character who does not like the squishiness of the race nor does he like the fact that he is studdered into being a Mage because of his stats. I was wondering what I could do to make him more of an assassin type character while still keeping his race. Thanks a bunch like always guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12036-story","name":"Story","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T11:38:27-08:00","id":1015318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015159-nagah-venom-holy-cow-also-kitsune-help#post1015159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello it's me again with that mixed breed chronicle I've been working on. This time I've sorted out everything regarding combat...well sorta I still need to structure my action better (newbie here). I have a few questions regarding my players characters.<br /> Firstly my Nagah player is enjoying his venom quite a bit. But I need ideas for how to challenge him as it seems like his venom does a lot of damage. I know that maybe normal, but it makes finding enemies for them fairly difficult if only he can poison them and kill them quickly.<br /> So any enemy suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nagah should be killing with extreme caution, on account of how they aren't supposed to exist. So if they do kill anyone with venom, they have to make the body disappear, or somehow erase any trace of the envenomation. Doing otherwise can get the character a mark over their heart, as a warning for wear the spear goes if they keep screwing up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly, I have a Kitsune character who does not like the squishiness of the race nor does he like the fact that he is studdered into being a Mage because of his stats. I was wondering what I could do to make him more of an assassin type character while still keeping his race. Thanks a bunch like always guys. </div> </div> </div>Tricking people. If you don't want squishy, don't play a fox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T13:51:53-08:00","id":1015360,"title":"","content":"Nagah venom kills could be potentially masked with more conventional poisons (a MA would detect that known poison and just assume that the victin was unusually susceptible). I can almost guarantee you that Nagah venom is not common enough for there to be any mundane test that detects it. In any case, who is going to know that it is Nagah venom and not fomori venom?<br /> <br /> As for Kitsune, they are supposed to be squishy. If he wanted an Assassin, he should have taken Ratkin, Hakken, Bastet, etc. If he wanted a tank, he should have taken anything else with the Silver Tolerance Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T16:52:34-08:00","id":1015410,"title":"","content":"If you're running non-traditional Nagah (which it sounds like you are), and the venom is a problem, use more spirits and vampires. Without the right gifts spirits are immune to the venom, and vampires only suffer half damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T17:42:39-08:00","id":1015424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015159-nagah-venom-holy-cow-also-kitsune-help?p=1015360#post1015360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nagah venom kills could be potentially masked with more conventional poisons (a MA would detect that known poison and just assume that the victin was unusually susceptible).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess not, since it's supposed to be a potential liability if relied upon. At least, that was something brought up frequently when the Nagah first cropped up (and were way more broken, since their claws and bite did Strength + 4 damage - in 2nd edition, mind - before you even took venom into account. Turns out it was like the Pumonca stats from the Bastet breedbook, though.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can almost guarantee you that Nagah venom is not common enough for there to be any mundane test that detects it. In any case, who is going to know that it is Nagah venom and not fomori venom? </div> </div> </div>Snake toxinologists and biochemists. And it wouldn't be at all out of left field for a sample of Nagah venom to get to such an expert if not cleaned up, especially if someone sees the two huge-ass viperine fang marks and notes the telltale discoloration around them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Kitsune, they are supposed to be squishy. If he wanted an Assassin, he should have taken Ratkin, Hakken, Bastet, etc. If he wanted a tank, he should have taken anything else with the Silver Tolerance Merit. </div> </div> </div>And hoped that the ST allowed said merit, too, I suppose. It's not a certain thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T19:23:41-08:00","id":1015478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015159-nagah-venom-holy-cow-also-kitsune-help?p=1015424#post1015424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And hoped that the ST allowed said merit, too, I suppose. It's not a certain thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only critter I allowed to have the silver tolerance merit was the Mokole, and that's because there is still gold to deal with...even then I wanted an explanation...<br /> <br /> On another note, Nagah venom is a hemotoxin...which doesn't exactly leave a clean body behind...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T20:43:43-08:00","id":1015513,"title":"","content":"Just chiming in, but death by Nagah venom is fairly distinctive. It does Agg and affect most supernatural creatures, so it is inherently supernatural. If bodies start showing up having been killed by such, it's going to be an incredibly distinct calling card. And that's something Nagah <i>need</i> to avoid.<br /> So at least on that end, the biting to kill enemies shouldn't be a go to move. But yea, their venom is really nasty. At least it only has a couple of doses a day, and can't be delivered in all forms.<br /> <br /> For the Kitsune, the squishiness is just something to deal with. At least they get to soak all types of damage, so it could be worse. For being an assassin, that should be a completely doable concept. Kitsune can learn other Changer's Gifts so if your player doesn't like the ones on his/her list, just give them access to some other ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T21:42:22-08:00","id":1015535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015159-nagah-venom-holy-cow-also-kitsune-help#post1015159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Secondly, I have a Kitsune character who does not like the squishiness of the race nor does he like the fact that he is studdered into being a Mage because of his stats. I was wondering what I could do to make him more of an assassin type character while still keeping his race. Thanks a bunch like always guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kitsune squishiness is highly overstated once they hit rank 2 and buy Enduring warrior. Now somepeople might say &quot;that's only on the Eiji list&quot; and that's true. However Kitsune learn &quot;off list&quot; gifts at the same xp as on list as long as they have a teacher so.. finding a kitsune who's willing to teach a gift that will keep fellow kitsune alive shouldn't be a hard thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Kitsune have a pretty good set of stealth stuff on their list and what they don't have they can get pretty easy, so building towards an assassin who gets in there and fades away is pretty solid but understand he needs to build for it. Strength is practically useless, anything mroe than 2 is a waste. Dex is your god stat. Stamina has some use on soak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T15:06:12-08:00","id":1015861,"title":"","content":"Kitsune would probably benefit from being snipers and poisoners over thugs. Mental primary (with Intelligence and Perception 4), physical secondary (with Dexterity 4), and social tertiary would be good for a Kitsune sniper/poisoner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T23:35:16-08:00","id":1016426,"title":"","content":"My Ananasi has venom just as virulent as Nagah venom (he actually used that as a guide). There is no consensus on whether snake or spider venom is overall more toxic to humans (&quot;most toxic venom&quot; does not necessarily mean &quot;most deadly&quot; - kills most number of humans - another species could be less toxic, but more numerous, so kill more humans, i.e. be more deadly) and my character comes from Phoneutria Fera (the deadliest spider venom known). So Nagah venom is not as distinct as some think and can be blamed on Ananasi. My ST throws a large population of Ratkin into the mix (that venom is desirable as all hell in the making of plagues, so my character must be careful not to just spill it anywhere, and Plague Lords have Gifts that can actually cause that venom to affect my character - nasty). Nagah can spit their venom, so blind enemies (BSDs, metis, battle scarred) can also present delivery problems, especially if they have an armoured exterior or can dodge (Ananasi in Crawlering form present special difficulties here).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T00:01:20-08:00","id":1016433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015159-nagah-venom-holy-cow-also-kitsune-help?p=1016426#post1016426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Ananasi has venom just as virulent as Nagah venom (he actually used that as a guide). There is no consensus on whether snake or spider venom is overall more toxic to humans (&quot;most toxic venom&quot; does not necessarily mean &quot;most deadly&quot; - kills most number of humans - another species could be less toxic, but more numerous, so kill more humans, i.e. be more deadly) and my character comes from Phoneutria Fera (the deadliest spider venom known). So Nagah venom is not as distinct as some think and can be blamed on Ananasi. My ST throws a large population of Ratkin into the mix (that venom is desirable as all hell in the making of plagues, so my character must be careful not to just spill it anywhere, and Plague Lords have Gifts that can actually cause that venom to affect my character - nasty). Nagah can spit their venom, so blind enemies (BSDs, metis, battle scarred) can also present delivery problems, especially if they have an armoured exterior or can dodge (Ananasi in Crawlering form present special difficulties here).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ananasi Venom is not supernatural though. It's just the &quot;normal&quot; venom of the kind of spider in question, upscaled in potence for Pithus form (almost certainly leaves a human dead or paralysed for hours depending on the species of spider), reduced potence (diluted compared to Pithus) in Lilian form, totaly normal in crawlerling form. That is unless any newer book contradicts the Ananasi breedbook there. They need gifts to make their venom effective against any supernatural creature.<br /> Standard (without influence from any special gifts), Ananasi venom is totally mundane (though possibly more dangerous because its potentially coming from a huge ass spider that carries a lot more of the stuff than her smaller siblings), doesn't cause any aggravated damage or effect supernaturals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T00:15:38-08:00","id":1016441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KItsune Litany</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I free you to do anything else necessary to achieve our goals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is important, Ratkin and Shadowlords look with envy on that level of pragmatism, Gaia commands you to cheat. Use guns. Make gun fetishes. Use Explosives. Everyone else has natural stuff so they can be called on as &quot;dishonorable&quot; but as a kitsune? You can use whatever.<br /> <br /> Cheat like you are pc. Honor is for Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T03:08:10-08:00","id":1016477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015159-nagah-venom-holy-cow-also-kitsune-help?p=1016433#post1016433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ananasi venom is totally mundane (though possibly more dangerous because its potentially coming from a huge ass spider that carries a lot more of the stuff than her smaller siblings), doesn't cause any aggravated damage or effect supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not the case anymore. &quot;Storytellers should determine for themselves the exact amount of damage dealt in each form (and any extra effects) based on the particular \u201cspider\u201d species, but venom <b>always deals aggravated damage</b> that can only be healed through medical attention or magical healing. Left unattended, the damage will never heal.&quot; (CB20)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T03:56:42-08:00","id":1016483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015159-nagah-venom-holy-cow-also-kitsune-help?p=1016477#post1016477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is not the case anymore. &quot;Storytellers should determine for themselves the exact amount of damage dealt in each form (and any extra effects) based on the particular \u201cspider\u201d species, but venom <b>always deals aggravated damage</b> that can only be healed through medical attention or magical healing. Left unattended, the damage will never heal.&quot; (CB20)</div> </div> </div> </div>oh thank you! I was totally unaware of that never having read that book. I had only the Breedbook to go by. Maybe I should try to get a look into the Ananasi part of that book somewhere as I'm playing an Ananasi character and it would be cool to see if a few things have been cleared up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T04:26:37-08:00","id":1016490,"title":"","content":"You're welcome Hexer, and I recommend the book. It has its flaws, but overall it is very good. I have a complete collection of breed books, and so I knew the former state of things, and how CB20 had altered them. CB20 does not do much to clarify Crawlerling form, sadly, which is where Ananasi need attention. It looks good on paper, but in practice things come up that the paper does not address. CB20 does keep the guideline about the different forms having different strength venoms, btw, &quot;Ananasi in Pithus form produce full strength venom; in Lilian form, their poison is somewhat diluted&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T16:07:56-08:00","id":1016786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015159-nagah-venom-holy-cow-also-kitsune-help?p=1015318#post1015318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nagah should be killing with extreme caution, on account of how they aren't supposed to exist. So if they do kill anyone with venom, they have to make the body disappear, or somehow erase any trace of the envenomation. Doing otherwise can get the character a mark over their heart, as a warning for wear the spear goes if they keep screwing up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Tricking people. If you don't want squishy, don't play a fox.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Shrug* Fair points. The Nagah in my game is non-tradional so I hadn't considered the social reprocussions of using his venom so much. Well, not compeletely true, I wanted him to have a flaw called &quot;Hunted&quot; after his character gained enough Renown as his fellow &quot;extinct&quot; Nagah go after him for basically revealing the fact that they still exist. The trouble comes with my players not being familar with the world of Werewolf the Apocalypse in general having never read the books. I wanted to make this type of revolation a surprise but that might not be a good idea for them since he is so proud of the potency of his character. Still, you guys have given me all kinds of ideas if I decide to continue this sub-plot for him.<br /> <br /> As for the Kitsune, my player just really wants to play a were-fox because that is the animal the apealed to him the most. So I was hoping to get more ideas about how I can make him the ninja-like character he'd like to play even if it is not optimal. One of the complaints that my players have is how their species of creature feels relagated to a certain class...nevermind that the true races are actually the Tribes of Werewolves and not really the other breeds imo. They just really insisted on not playing werewolves...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\">Aya Tari</a>[/B]]<br /> As for Kitsune, they are supposed to be squishy. If he wanted an Assassin, he should have taken Ratkin, Hakken, Bastet, etc. If he wanted a tank, he should have taken anything else with the Silver Tolerance Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, he wanted to play a were-fox more than the &quot;class&quot; itself. I just wanted ideas on how to make it more fun for him. Have his cake and eat it too if it is at all possible. First I've heard of that merit though...I'm gonna make sure none of them get it. :P<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're running non-traditional Nagah (which it sounds like you are), and the venom is a problem, use more spirits and vampires. Without the right gifts spirits are immune to the venom, and vampires only suffer half damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whelp, I guess that was pretty obvious huh? xD I'm going to go ahead an write up some banes, spirits, and undead they can battle. Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kitsune squishiness is highly overstated once they hit rank 2 and buy Enduring warrior. Now somepeople might say &quot;that's only on the Eiji list&quot; and that's true. However Kitsune learn &quot;off list&quot; gifts at the same xp as on list as long as they have a teacher so.. finding a kitsune who's willing to teach a gift that will keep fellow kitsune alive shouldn't be a hard thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\">Aya Tari</a>[/B]]<br /> Kitsune have a pretty good set of stealth stuff on their list and what they don't have they can get pretty easy, so building towards an assassin who gets in there and fades away is pretty solid but understand he needs to build for it. Strength is practically useless, anything mroe than 2 is a waste. Dex is your god stat. Stamina has some use on soak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kitsune would probably benefit from being snipers and poisoners over thugs. Mental primary (with Intelligence and Perception 4), physical secondary (with Dexterity 4), and social tertiary would be good for a Kitsune sniper/poisoner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks you two, this was exactly what I was looking for! I went ahead and jotted those tips that down for him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\">idpersona</a>[/B]]<br /> For the Kitsune, the squishiness is just something to deal with. At least they get to soak all types of damage, so it could be worse. For being an assassin, that should be a completely doable concept. Kitsune can learn other Changer's Gifts so if your player doesn't like the ones on his/her list, just give them access to some other ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I keep going back and forth over if I want to forgo the &quot;non-healing&quot; thing. I mean...I already have a non-traditional Nagah, I could do the same for him. But even if I do, I just don't see him being par to par with the Nagah and the other player the Khan no matter what. So I think he...if he wants...should fit a different type of role for the group. He already is, seeing as he is the only so far that can do anything involving the Umbra or magic in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12036-story","user":"Story","date":". 12-13-2016, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12036-story","name":"Story","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T21:41:55-08:00","id":1016907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015159-nagah-venom-holy-cow-also-kitsune-help?p=1016786#post1016786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I keep going back and forth over if I want to forgo the &quot;non-healing&quot; thing. I mean...I already have a non-traditional Nagah, I could do the same for him. But even if I do, I just don't see him being par to par with the Nagah and the other player the Khan no matter what. So I think he...if he wants...should fit a different type of role for the group. He already is, seeing as he is the only so far that can do anything involving the Umbra or magic in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a couple of follow up thoughts. First, if you and your player don't like the idea of Kitsune not having Regeneration, then change it. That's a relatively minor aspect of the Kitsune imo. You could also just give the player a merit (say 7 points) that says that they have Regeneration, even if other Kitsune don't.<br /> There is some precedent for that in my mind when comparing it to sidestepping. Some Fera can't sidestep, but can either take a 7 point merit or a 2nd or 4th rank Gift to do so. So that is another solution.<br /> <br /> Now, on the player comparing their fox character in combat to the tiger or the giant viper...well in toe to toe combat, it's going to be hard to stack up. Kitsune have a lot of strengths though. I'm assuming you're using CB20. Kitsune get a reduced Per dif in all forms outside of homid. And they get decent to great Dex bonuses. And Dex is one of the best stats.A high Dex character can generally get more successes, and as such more damage. The Per bonus in Koto can also add to aiming Firearms. And since their war form isn't terribly huge, they should be able to wield most guns with little issue (and if there was an issue, Rite of Dedication would fix that too).<br /> <br /> Kistune get to learn Gifts from pretty much everyone, so steal away to round out the character concept. If the Kitune want's to buff their soak, learn the Khan Gift Crushing the Centipede (original Hengeyokai book) and then just use the block defensive maneuver. The Gift adds 5 soak and lasts a turn per success on activation (and is Rank 1). A bunch of the Ratkin Gifts would work well for a Kitsune. I personally love Sticky Paws for guaranteed disarming people (you roll a Dex based roll against the victim's Dex +3). These are just some ideas. It's important to remember that if a Fera doesn't have a physical predisposition for a Gift (like Cat Eyes for Bastet) then the Gift should be able to be stolen at Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T22:19:12-08:00","id":1016914,"title":"","content":"The soak bonus only applies to the hands and feet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T22:29:15-08:00","id":1016916,"title":"","content":"Yep. That's why I said to block. It's still one of the only Rank 1 Gifts to add to soak, and it adds a significant amount. But it is obviously circumstantial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T01:36:55-08:00","id":1016946,"title":"","content":"About the Kitsune problem: you talked about that he doesn't like the squishiness and wants to be more the Ninja/Assassin type.<br /> Just to clarify: what is it that you (or your player) are trying to achieve here?<br /> <br /> Personally I'd say a Ninja/Assassin might very well be squishy as the concept doesn't strike me as a straight up warrior type. Are you trying to make him more &quot;tanky&quot; to be able to fight more effectively alongside the Kahn and Nagah (&quot;in the main line&quot;) or are you more going for a sneaky guy that attacks for effect when the opportunity arises and trys to stay away from damage when it doesn't?<br /> <br /> As an example, here is our current group:<br /> - A Kitsune (Pillar) that aims more for the sneaky and support tasks. His biggest advantage in combat is a fetish jacket with extendable sleeves and a relatively high strength-rating of its own (can't remember what its called exactly but it has a monkey-spirit in it). In fights he tries to stay out of the main brawl and support where possible.<br /> - A Tengu (Leave) who spies and sneaks on stuff, is a great asset for us in getting an idea what we're dealing with with his gifts and also aspires to be a sword-master. I think we haven't had much combat yet since he joined so...<br /> - A Tengu (Mirror) who specializes in Umbra and spirit stuff. She isn't a great combatant (except in the Umbra) and knows it so what she does most in fights is to either do her own thing or provide distractions and opening up advantages for the rest like doing a quick hit-and-run attack in raven form going for someones face or something.<br /> - A Same-Bito (Fist) who is our main fighter in combat. He is kinda big on honour so prefers straight up fights and can pull it off much better than most of the group, too. He is the tanky bastard who can also deal out tons of damage with good rolls (and at least a solid amount otherwise). Most of us cant compete with him in straight up combat and we know it so we let him do his thing in this regard.<br /> - An Ananasi (Lantern, my own character) who in a fight is usually the second main combatant as he is more geared towards it than everyone else except the Same-Bito. As he doesn't have the resilience of the whereshark and also has a much harder time regenerating (Ananasi also have no regeneration and only heal using blood which they also need to power pretty much anything else) as well as a whole different philosophy he uses a different approach though. He has to rely on speed and dexterity (where he has high boni) to avoid damage and also doesn't usually like a simple straight up fight if it can be avoided. In combat he usually aims more for sneakiness and good positioning to get in swift, devastating blows when the opportunity arises.<br /> Where the Same-Bito is more the straight up fighter who might exchange blows with an opponent until one drops (which he's really good at), the Ananasi is more the &quot;try not to get hit at all and aim to get that single, well-placed strike in that will end the confrontation (or just trap an opponent and strike from the shadows if that is an option)&quot; type.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is: we all approach combat differently. Some are more use in a fight than others but everyone usually finds something to do (even if it is NOT fighting and doing something else useful if possible) and even those who do fight go about it quite differently. Some are more straight fighters, others more the assassin type who can be squishy and still &quot;do their job&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}